"centred"><Image height="87" width="222" zoomable="false" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjLCQtJSZGbG9hdEc2IyUpaW5maW5pdHlHISIiLSUpQk9VTkRTX1lHRictJS1CT1VORFNfV0lEVEhHRictJS5CT1VORFNfSEVJR0hUR0YnLSUpQ0hJTERSRU5HNiI=</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">c) Give the total number of iterations</Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"><Image height="92" width="122" zoomable="false" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjLCQtJSZGbG9hdEc2IyUpaW5maW5pdHlHISIiLSUpQk9VTkRTX1lHRictJS1CT1VORFNfV0lEVEhHRictJS5CT1VORFNfSEVJR0hUR0YnLSUpQ0hJTERSRU5HNiI=</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">d) Give the final, converged position and velocity</Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"><Image height="171" width="561" zoomable="false" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjLCQtJSZGbG9hdEc2IyUpaW5maW5pdHlHISIiLSUpQk9VTkRTX1lHRictJS1CT1VORFNfV0lEVEhHRictJS5CT1VORFNfSEVJR0hUR0YnLSUpQ0hJTERSRU5HNiI=</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">e) Plot the top view of the final trajectory and the overlay with final position of each iteration</Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"><Image height="347" width="685" zoomable="false" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjJCIjNSEiIi0lKUJPVU5EU19ZRzYjJCIiIUYqLSUtQk9VTkRTX1dJRFRIRzYjJCIlcW9GKi0lLkJPVU5EU19IRUlHSFRHNiMkIiUhXCRGKi0lKUNISUxEUkVORzYi</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"><Image height="340" width="674" zoomable="false" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjJCIjNSEiIi0lKUJPVU5EU19ZRzYjJCIiIUYqLSUtQk9VTkRTX1dJRFRIRzYjJCIlZ25GKi0lLkJPVU5EU19IRUlHSFRHNiMkIiU/TUYqLSUpQ0hJTERSRU5HNiI=</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">g) Experiment with different trust regions</Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"><Image height="375" width="661" zoomable="false" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjJCIjNSEiIi0lKUJPVU5EU19ZRzYjJCIiIUYqLSUtQk9VTkRTX1dJRFRIRzYjJCIlSW1GKi0lLkJPVU5EU19IRUlHSFRHNiMkIiVxUEYqLSUpQ0hJTERSRU5HNiI=</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" alignment="centred">The experiment with different trust regions for the same problem is exactly as it sounds. All other parameters consistent, the trust region was changed to observe how the number of iterations would change. The y-axis is the cost function, rmiss norm over r0 norm, and the x-axis is the number of iterations to converge. As expected the smaller the trust region, the more iteration it is going to take to converge, however, the 0.1 Trust region never actually converges with the precision the other TRs have, and TR of 0.05 outperforms TR of 0.01 on number of iterations.</Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"><Font underline="true" bold="true">Problem 3</Font></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Reference final position and B at t = 8 TU. These are in line with results on homework assignment:</Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"><Image height="295" width="585" zoomable="false" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjLCQtJSZGbG9hdEc2IyUpaW5maW5pdHlHISIiLSUpQk9VTkRTX1lHRictJS1CT1VORFNfV0lEVEhHRictJS5CT1VORFNfSEVJR0hUR0YnLSUpQ0hJTERSRU5HNiI=</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">a) D submatrix at t = 6 TU</Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"><Image height="125" width="571" zoomable="false" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjLCQtJSZGbG9hdEc2IyUpaW5maW5pdHlHISIiLSUpQk9VTkRTX1lHRictJS1CT1VORFNfV0lEVEhHRictJS5CT1VORFNfSEVJR0hUR0YnLSUpQ0hJTERSRU5HNiI=</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">b) Total scalar delta-v required </Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"><Image height="77" width="217" zoomable="false" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjLCQtJSZGbG9hdEc2IyUpaW5maW5pdHlHISIiLSUpQk9VTkRTX1lHRictJS1CT1VORFNfV0lEVEhHRictJS5CT1VORFNfSEVJR0hUR0YnLSUpQ0hJTERSRU5HNiI=</Drawing-Root></Image> <Image height="73" width="182" zoomable="false" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjLCQtJSZGbG9hdEc2IyUpaW5maW5pdHlHISIiLSUpQk9VTkRTX1lHRictJS1CT1VORFNfV0lEVEhHRictJS5CT1VORFNfSEVJR0hUR0YnLSUpQ0hJTERSRU5HNiI=</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">c) Plot of the reference and truth trajectories overlayed with delta-vs</Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"><Image height="365" width="592" zoomable="false" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjJCIjNSEiIi0lKUJPVU5EU19ZRzYjJCIiIUYqLSUtQk9VTkRTX1dJRFRIRzYjJCIlU2ZGKi0lLkJPVU5EU19IRUlHSFRHNiMkIiVxT0YqLSUpQ0hJTERSRU5HNiI=</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">d) Plot of the relative trajectory</Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"><Image height="412" width="645" zoomable="false" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjJCIjNSEiIi0lKUJPVU5EU19ZRzYjJCIiIUYqLSUtQk9VTkRTX1dJRFRIRzYjJCIlcWtGKi0lLkJPVU5EU19IRUlHSFRHNiMkIiVTVEYqLSUpQ0hJTERSRU5HNiI=</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">e) Plot of the magnitude of the delta position versus time</Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"><Image height="409" width="650" zoomable="false" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjJCIjNSEiIi0lKUJPVU5EU19ZRzYjJCIiIUYqLSUtQk9VTkRTX1dJRFRIRzYjJCIlP2xGKi0lLkJPVU5EU19IRUlHSFRHNiMkIiU1VEYqLSUpQ0hJTERSRU5HNiI=</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">f) Plot of the magnitude of the maneuvers versus time</Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"><Image height="418" width="647" zoomable="false" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjJCIjNSEiIi0lKUJPVU5EU19ZRzYjJCIiIUYqLSUtQk9VTkRTX1dJRFRIRzYjJCIlIVwnRiotJS5CT1VORFNfSEVJR0hURzYjJCIlK1VGKi0lKUNISUxEUkVORzYi</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">g) Final position and velocity of the truth trajectory</Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"><Image height="272" width="227" zoomable="false" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjLCQtJSZGbG9hdEc2IyUpaW5maW5pdHlHISIiLSUpQk9VTkRTX1lHRictJS1CT1VORFNfV0lEVEhHRictJS5CT1VORFNfSEVJR0hUR0YnLSUpQ0hJTERSRU5HNiI=</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">h) Experiment with different strategies and values of GM</Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"><Image height="444" width="680" zoomable="false" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjJCIjNSEiIi0lKUJPVU5EU19ZRzYjJCIiIUYqLSUtQk9VTkRTX1dJRFRIRzYjJCIlP29GKi0lLkJPVU5EU19IRUlHSFRHNiMkIiVnV0YqLSUpQ0hJTERSRU5HNiI=</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" alignment="centred">The above graphic shows how changing GM effects the magnitude difference in the position at each 1 TU timestep. The best performing GMs was oddly enough the 1.05 with the worst being 1.25. The GM of 1 and 1.25 don't even converge like the rest do to the reference trajectory final position. Interestingly, GM=1 does not perform well because the model is build to update and perturbate, but there is no need with GM=1 so the additional error compiles. The smaller GMs generally are better performing the acceleration is weighted less in the EOMs.</Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"><Image height="512" width="685" zoomable="false" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjJCIjNSEiIi0lKUJPVU5EU19ZRzYjJCIiIUYqLSUtQk9VTkRTX1dJRFRIRzYjJCIlcW9GKi0lLkJPVU5EU19IRUlHSFRHNiMkIiVTXkYqLSUpQ0hJTERSRU5HNiI=</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" alignment="centred">This experiment shows again the magnitude delta position versus time with the interval times changing. the best performing intTime is still 1, this is likely due to the numerical error that compiles the more iterations that are run. </Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field>
